  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/puc900.html",
  "prefLabel": "Puc 902.15 Generating Capacity",
  "priorExpiration": "2014-07-02",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Puc 902.15 “Generating Capacity” means, for inverter-based units, the maximum generating capacity alternating current kilowatt rating of the inverters, and for other interconnections, the nameplate capacity kilowatt rating of the generating facility.\n\nSource. #9998, eff 9-20-11 (from Puc 902.09); ss by #10502, INTERIM, eff 1-3-14, EXPIRED: 7-2-14\n\nNew. #10757, eff 1-8-15 (from Puc 902.14); ss by #13080, eff 9-14-20 (formerly Puc 902.10)",
